Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/albrhi-repo
Description: Save any video, photo or GIF — no ads, no Grok, less tracking. Arabic or English.
 .
 X does not decide what to show you in the screens themselves. It asks one place —
 its own list of switches — and every part of the app obeys the answer. This tweak sits
 at that one place.
 .
 ▍SAVE VIDEOS, PHOTOS AND GIFS
 A download button sits on the video itself, in the corner beside play and mute. Tap it and
 the video is in Photos, at the best quality X offers. Photos save at the size they were
 uploaded — not the smaller one the timeline was showing you.
 .
 And a list under a two-finger hold holds everything X has shown you since you opened it,
 newest first — the same save, from the model rather than a button, so it keeps working on
 a build where X has renamed the video view.
 .
 ▍WHAT IT SHOWS
 Every switch the app asked about while you were using it, the answer it was given, and
 how many times it asked. Nothing is guessed and nothing is written down in advance: the
 list is whatever your copy of X actually looked up on your phone.
 .
 ▍READY-MADE FEATURES
 Twenty-seven switches in plain language: hide ads, hide the Promote button, hide Grok, stop
 X translating by itself, hide Premium ads, send less about you, clean up the interface,
 hide view counts, hide Spaces, stop GIFs playing alone, pinch to zoom in the timeline,
 more gestures, more tabs, keep your likes private, open faster, and more. Each one sets a
 group of X's own switches at once, and each says what it does before you turn it on.
 .
 ▍OR ANSWER ANY SWITCH YOURSELF
 Tap any switch in the list and set it on or off. Your own answer always beats a feature,
 and one button undoes everything.
 .
 ▍HOW TO OPEN IT
 Hold two fingers anywhere in X.
 .
 ▍WHY THIS WAY
 Other tweaks change a screen at a time, and stop working the day X renames that screen.
 This one sits where X makes the decision, so it keeps working when the screens change.
 .
 TESTED ON X 12.14 and 12.15. Nothing is pinned to a version number: every class is looked up at
 runtime and skipped if it is not there.
 .
 Every switch a feature touches is one a real phone reported. What each one does is read
 from its name, so if something looks wrong, turn the feature off and X goes straight back
 to normal.
 .
 The switch layer was found from the published work of BandarHL (BHTwitter) and
 TWIGalaxy, whose choice of where to hook this app is credited. No code is taken from
 either. The timeline section filter, the typing-indicator and screenshot switches, the
 number displays and the interface switches follow NeoFreeBird by orionblur, a GPLv3
 BHTwitter fork written against newer X builds, carried over under the same licence.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Open source under the GNU GPL v3.
